{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of unordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"{u, v}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the same edge as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"{v, u}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot (none while the vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":" in order, each its own slot). Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". Each slot has a row of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the slots of its neighbors and a parallel row of the positions of its incident edges; each edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is in both its endpoints’ rows, and a self-loop twice in its vertex’s row (as Boost stores it)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The rows share one array per kind, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"many vertices it has. A hash table from unordered slot pair to position (open addressing with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplicative hash, not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":"’s SipHash) answers "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1) expected."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each edge keeps the orientation it was first inserted with.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/UndirectedAdjacencyList.swift#L24"},"externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule010UndirectedaB0V","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentat